\ The raise from tail_boundary_fallback_caller.1z with `boom`'s effect declared, pinned eager. Both
\ sides of the boundary now compile. The chain carries a row the interpreted chain in
\ tail_boundary_compiled_caller.1z does not.
\
\ The compiled `go` tail-calls `when` through its fallback boundary, which drops the `when` row as
\ the interpreter does. The `if` inside `when` runs the arm inline, and the compiled `boom` there
\ raises rather than being tail-called, so the `if` frame is pended. The interpreted chain is the
\ target.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ boom ] when ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
